# The Haven's leaders, the hub (docs/DIALOGUE.md, "Hubs: work comes out of talk"): work, the news
# and what they make of you come out of talk. Each topic carries a built reply (call:slot:N): 0 the
# job (their own, else the stronghold's contracts), 1 the built news, 2 what they make of you.
# Voice: warm, worried, practical, darkly funny sideways. The List is said sideways, never announced.
# Work talk explains the work (what, where, who for, the pay, the danger) before the accept.

conv haven.leader.work_food
for stronghold:haven, seat:haven/council_head
when need:food & !exiled
topic "Why are the bowls half full?"
prio ask
voice haven

bind short = house:nearest_short

node start
  jump route:out -> other_route
  jump epilogue -> after
  say? stronghold :: This is the chair's table, and the soup on it is mostly a rumour. Every Haven house sends me its count, and every count is thinner than it says.
  say? trait:merciful :: Sit down first. You look like the soup. Stores are low, love. Lower than we tell the children, and the children can count.
  say? trait:pragmatist :: Food in, food out. Lately it's mostly out. I can do the sums. I'd rather not, because the sums have names in them.
  say We're down to the tins with no labels. We open one at supper and find out what we're eating. Last night it was peaches. Nobody complained.
  say? bound:short :: {bind:short} has gone to half portions. They haven't said so on the radio, which is how I know.
  say? night :: And it's night, which is when people lie awake counting what's left.
  say Nothing comes in from outside. Every tin here, somebody found in a cupboard or carried down a road. We'll manage. We always say that, and mostly we do.
  > @who Who's short, exactly? -> who
  > @why Why not ask Bastion for rations? -> bastion
  > @worth What would I get out of it? -> worth
  > @nurse Who's eating least? It shows first. -> nurse   if bg:nurse,doctor,elder
  > @help Is there something I can do? -> offer
  > @no Not today. -> hub

node who
  say? bound:short :: {bind:short} first. Then the rest of them, one by one, like lights going off down a street.
  say Everyone. Some just say it louder.
  say? supply:lost :: The last truck didn't come. Nobody's saying why, which means somebody knows.
  say It's never the food that runs out first. It's the patience. Then people start saying mouths when they mean the old and the sick.
  > @help2 Then let me help. -> offer
  > @back1 Let me ask something else. -> hub

node bastion
  say? truce:bastion :: We've a truce with Bastion just now. A truce isn't a larder. They're counting their own tins, and their tins have serial numbers.
  say? feud:bastion :: Ask Bastion? We're feuding with them this week. They'd ask what's in it for them, then come round and count us.
  say They'd feed us, for a list of names. Who's in each house, who can work, who can carry a rifle. We don't hand out lists.
  say Some of their posts send a crate back to our houses against orders. Bless them. It's never enough, and they get in trouble for it.
  > @help3 Then let me help instead. -> offer
  > @back2 Let me ask something else. -> hub

node worth
  say? trait:merciful :: Supper. A bed. People who'll remember your face kindly. It's what we've got, and we'll give you all of it.
  say Haven Favor, which buys bandages and tins at our stores. A hot meal. And a name the houses say nicely. Don't laugh. Out here that's money.
  > @help4 Fair. What's the job? -> offer
  > @dry4 Supper it is, then. -> offer   dry
  > @back3 Let me think about it. -> hub

node nurse
  say The old ones. They pass their bowls along when nobody's looking, and then they're the ones looking thin at the next count.
  say You noticed. Most people only notice the children. The children are fine. We make sure the children are fine.
  > @help5 Let me help with the food. -> offer
  > @back4 Let me ask something else. -> hub

node offer
  say It's carrying, mostly. Food to a house that's short, medicine from a town the dead got to first, people walked in off a bad road to one of our doors.
  say It pays Haven Favor and a meal. The roads aren't safe, so don't be a hero about it. If it goes wrong, come back. We'd rather have you than the tins.
  say? tier:haven>=trusted :: I'd hoped you'd ask. I've a list. Of course I've a list.
  > @take I'll do it. Tell me where. -> hub   do call:slot:0
  > @risk How dangerous are the roads now? -> risk
  > @later Let me think about it. -> hub

node risk
  say The dead are slow, but there are a lot of them, and they come to noise. The Red Hand are quick, and there are fewer of them, and they come to tins.
  say Go in daylight, go quiet, and if a house has no bear on its door and you can hear something behind it, keep walking.
  > @take4 All right. I'll do it. -> hub   do call:slot:0
  > @later4 Not today, then. -> hub

node other_route
  say You're with another lot now, for the cure. I heard. You'll still be fed here. We've fed people who picked worse.
  say People still need feeding, whoever you march with, and the work pays the same Favor.
  > @take2 Is there still work for me? -> hub   do call:slot:0
  > @back5 Let me ask something else. -> hub

node after
  say? cure_held:haven :: We hold the cure, and we're handing it out house by house, and the stores haven't noticed any of it. People still eat every day.
  say The cure's out, or near enough, and the soup hasn't heard. People still eat every day, and the barriers stay closed until processing.
  > @take3 Then I'll keep working for you. -> hub   do call:slot:0
  > @back6 Let me ask something else. -> hub

conv haven.leader.work
for stronghold:haven, seat:haven/council_head
when !need:food & !exiled
topic "What's keeping you up at night?"
prio ask
voice haven

bind over = news:overrun
bind burned = news:burned

node start
  jump route:out -> other_route
  jump epilogue -> after
  say? need:security & bound:over :: {bind:over} went to the dead. That's close enough to hear on a still night, and every house knows it.
  say? need:security :: The fences. Every house thinks its fence is fine until something leans on it at three in the morning.
  say? need:people :: Empty beds. We've more beds than people now. People don't leave the Haven. They stop arriving.
  say? need:supplies :: Bandages boiled and boiled again. Batteries. Thread. The small things keep a house alive, and we're out of the small things.
  say? bound:burned :: {bind:burned} burned, and nobody put it out. The families from there will be at our doors by morning, and we'll make room.
  say It's quiet. Quiet is when things go missing, and people, and nobody notices until the count at supper.
  say? rain :: And the roof in the east room leaks. That's not the worst of it, only the loudest.
  say? finale:open :: And everyone's picking a side for the cure, as if the soup will wait for them to decide.
  say? trait:talker :: I'd tell you the rest, but then you'd know as much as me, and I'd have nothing left to trade for gossip.
  say Same as always, love. Too many people need too many things, and I'm the one they ask.
  > @what What happened there? -> place   if bound:over
  > @burnt Who's taking the burned-out families? -> families   if bound:burned
  > @fences Who's watching your fences? -> fences
  > @elder You've seen worse than this. Say it. -> told   if bg:elder
  > @press Tell me what you're not saying. -> told | half | half   check persuade haven 2 easier:merciful harder:paranoid bg:elder,nurse
  > @help Is there anything I can do? -> offer

node place
  say The dead came in through the back gardens, the way they do. The people left by the front, the way we taught them.
  say Some got to us. Some didn't. We'll read their names at supper and light the candles.
  > @help2 Then let me help. -> offer
  > @back1 I'm sorry. Something else. -> hub

node families
  say We are. Of course we are. Where else would they go? We'll squeeze: two to a mattress, the children in the hall.
  say Squeezing is a skill. We've had a lot of practice since Day 2.
  > @help3 Let me help with that. -> offer
  > @back2 Let me ask something else. -> hub

node fences
  say? need:security :: Children and old men, in shifts. They're good at shouting. Shouting isn't a fence, but it wakes the people who can hold one.
  say Whoever's awake. That's the rota here: being awake, and having a torch.
  > @help4 I could stand a watch for you. -> offer
  > @back3 Let me ask something else. -> hub

node told
  say? major:every_name :: The council's arguing about the List again. Who's on it, who comes off when the stores run short. Every house has an opinion and a pencil.
  say The council argues about who gets the next bed: the family off the road, or the man who can fix a pump. It's not the arguing that keeps me up. It's that they're both right.
  do learn:haven.council_argues:6h
  > @help5 Then give me something useful to do. -> offer
  > @back4 Thank you for saying it. -> hub

node half
  say Nothing you'd sleep better for knowing. Ask me again when you've eaten here a few times and I know what you do with what you hear.
  > @help6 Then give me something to do. -> offer
  > @back5 Fair enough. Something else. -> hub

node offer
  say There's always something. Water and wood carried, a fence mended, somebody fetched home off a road, medicine from a town the dead got to first.
  say It pays Haven Favor and a hot meal, and the houses remember who helped. Some of it means going where the dead are. I'll tell you which before you go.
  say? trait:merciful :: Eat first, mind. Then work. That's the order here, whatever the council says.
  > @take I'll do it. Where do I start? -> hub   do call:slot:0
  > @later Let me think about it. -> hub

node other_route
  say You're walking with another lot now, for the cure. Fine. People here still need things doing, whoever you march with.
  > @take2 Is there still work for me? -> hub   do call:slot:0
  > @back6 Let me ask something else. -> hub

node after
  say The cure's done, and people still fall off roofs and run out of thread. Grief has a lot of chores, and the barriers stay closed until processing.
  > @take3 Then I'll keep working for you. -> hub   do call:slot:0
  > @back7 Let me ask something else. -> hub

conv haven.leader.news
for stronghold:haven, seat:haven/council_head
when !exiled
topic "What are the houses saying?"
prio world
voice haven

bind took = news:taken
bind who = news:taken_by
bind from = news:taken_from
bind dead = news:leader_dead
bind horde = news:horde
bind hungry = news:hungry
bind gone = news:emptied
bind saved = news:rescue

node start
  jump news:leader_dead -> dead
  jump news:emptied -> emptied
  jump news:taken -> taken
  jump news:horde -> horde
  jump news:rescue -> rescue
  jump news:hungry -> hungry
  say? epilogue :: The houses are saying goodbye to each other. On the radio, in letters, in tins left on each other's doorsteps.
  say? cure>=75 :: The houses are saying the lab's close to the cure. Close is a word that's been close for weeks.
  say? outbreak:overrun :: The houses are saying the roads belong to the dead now. We go out in twos, and we come back in twos, or we don't go.
  say The houses are saying what houses say. Who coughed, who's courting, who took the last of the jam and blamed the mice.
  say? !night & hour<11 :: Morning gossip's the kindest. People haven't slept on it yet.
  > @mine And what are they saying about me? -> me
  > @more What else is going round? -> hub   do call:slot:1
  > @back0 Let me ask something else. -> hub

node dead
  say {bind:dead} is dead. We heard it from three houses before the radio said it, and the radio had it wrong.
  say? trait:merciful :: Whoever they were to you, their name gets read at supper tonight. We don't skip anyone.
  say Whatever else they were, they kept people alive. That earns a name read out and a candle in the window.
  > @who2 Who takes their place? -> place
  > @more1 What else is going round? -> hub   do call:slot:1
  > @back1 Let me ask something else. -> hub

node place
  say Whoever stands up first and doesn't sit down again. That's how it went last time, and that's how it goes.
  > @more2 What else is going round? -> hub   do call:slot:1
  > @back2 Let me ask something else. -> hub

node emptied
  say The last of them left the house in {bind:gone}. They took the bear off the door and carried it with them.
  say Somebody will paint it again on a door here. We've a lot of bears now.
  > @where Where did they all go? -> went
  > @more3 What else is going round? -> hub   do call:slot:1
  > @back3 Let me ask something else. -> hub

node went
  say Here. The next house over. Wherever there's a bowl. We don't turn people from the door. That's the one rule we've kept all the way through.
  > @more4 What else is going round? -> hub   do call:slot:1
  > @back4 Let me ask something else. -> hub

node taken
  say They're saying {bind:who} took {bind:took} from {bind:from}. Fighting over a town nobody can live in.
  say? truce:redhand :: We've a truce with the Red Hand, so I'm told to say nothing about them. I'm saying nothing very loudly.
  say Whoever holds it, the families there still need feeding, and they'll still come to us when it goes wrong.
  > @true Is that true? -> sure
  > @more5 What else is going round? -> hub   do call:slot:1
  > @back5 Let me ask something else. -> hub

node sure
  say As true as anything said over soup. Someone's cousin saw the flag change from a roof. Cousins are very reliable about flags.
  > @more6 What else is going round? -> hub   do call:slot:1
  > @back6 Let me ask something else. -> hub

node horde
  say A crowd of the dead came through near {bind:horde}. Somebody rang a bell or ran a generator, and they came to see.
  say Tell people, if you pass a house: quiet is a kindness now. Noise is a dinner bell.
  > @more7 What else is going round? -> hub   do call:slot:1
  > @back7 I'll tell them. Something else. -> hub

node rescue
  say Someone brought people in alive at {bind:saved}. Alive. Every house heard it by supper, and some of them cried.
  say? helped :: Some say it was you. I didn't correct them.
  say That's the good kind of gossip. We run short of it.
  > @more8 What else is going round? -> hub   do call:slot:1
  > @back8 Let me ask something else. -> hub

node hungry
  say {bind:hungry} is on half portions. They say it isn't, which is how you know.
  say The Haven doesn't blame. We send tins, when we have tins. When we don't, somebody walks over with a pot and an excuse.
  > @more9 What else is going round? -> hub   do call:slot:1
  > @back9 Let me ask something else. -> hub

node me
  jump kit:other -> me_colours
  jump best:haven -> me_known
  say? tier:haven>=trusted :: That you're one of ours, near enough. That you eat with your hat off. Small things. They count.
  say? fresh :: That there's a new face. People are kind to a new face for a day or two. Use it well.
  say Not much yet. That's not a bad thing. The ones the houses talk about are mostly trouble, or dead.
  > @back10 Good to know. Something else. -> hub

node me_known
  say That you {best}. They say it at supper, with the bread. That's the best place in the Haven to be said.
  > @back11 That's kind. Something else. -> hub

node me_colours
  say That you came in wearing someone else's colours. People notice colours. They're polite about it, to your face.
  > @back12 Let me ask something else. -> hub

conv haven.leader.me
for stronghold:haven, seat:haven/council_head
when !exiled
topic "Am I welcome here?"
prio reaction
voice haven

node start
  jump kit:other -> colours
  jump bite_shown -> bitten
  jump infamy:haven>=15 -> infamous
  jump tier:haven>=trusted -> trusted
  jump tier:haven>=known -> known
  say? fresh :: You've the look of someone who's just been told the house rules and is still deciding which ones count. They all count.
  say Welcome's a big word. You're fed and you're inside. That's most of it. The rest is what you do while you're here.
  > @more Where do I stand with you, honestly? -> hub   do call:slot:2
  > @fair Fair enough. -> hub

node colours
  say? kit:full :: Head to boot in someone else's kit, in my house. I'll assume you're cold and not lost.
  say You're wearing their colours. We don't shoot through doors with bears on them. Don't make us reconsider.
  > @explain It was what I could find. -> found
  > @more1 Where do I stand with you? -> hub   do call:slot:2
  > @back1 Let me ask something else. -> hub

node found
  say Everything is, these days. Take it off before supper, love. The children ask questions, and they ask them loudly.
  > @back2 I'll change before supper. -> hub

node bitten
  say Show me the arm. No. Don't. I can see it from here.
  say? declared :: You told the house. That's why you're still inside, and why nobody's moved their chair away from you. That's the whole of the rule.
  say Tell the house before it tells us. Declare it out loud, and the medic will do what can be done. That's the one thing we ask.
  > @more2 Am I still welcome, then? -> hub   do call:slot:2
  > @back3 I'll see the medic. -> hub

node infamous
  say? worst:haven :: People here know you {worst}. They're polite about it. That's how you know it's serious.
  say People go quiet when you come in. That's not a welcome. That's a habit we learned on the roads.
  > @more3 Say it straight. Where do I stand? -> hub   do call:slot:2
  > @back4 Let me ask something else. -> hub

node trusted
  say? best:haven :: You {best}. You'll be welcome here when there's nothing left to welcome you with.
  say? title:haven :: They call you {title:haven} in the houses. They don't call many people anything.
  say You're one of the people I don't count the bowls against. You won't know how rare that is.
  > @more4 Where do I stand, in full? -> hub   do call:slot:2
  > @back5 Thank you. Something else. -> hub

node known
  say? helped :: You helped us. People remember who helped. We've no other way to pay that's worth anything.
  say? jobs:haven>=3 :: You've done a few jobs for us now. The houses have started saying your name without a question mark after it.
  say You're known here. Known is good. Known means someone would notice if you didn't come back.
  > @more5 And where do I stand overall? -> hub   do call:slot:2
  > @back6 Good. Let me ask something else. -> hub
